# Clear Commit Messages

Hakimo rule (ثابتة): كل كوميت لازم يكون واضح.

## Required

- Subject explains **why** / outcome in plain language (1 line, ~72 chars).
- Prefer conventional prefixes used in this repo: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `chore:`.
- Body optional; use for scope notes or risk — not a file dump.

## Forbidden

- Generic automation spam: `ship: auto release after agent work`
- Vague subjects: `update`, `fixes`, `wip`, `changes`
- Mentions of the agent/tool instead of the product change

## When using ship pipeline

Set a clear message explicitly:

```bash
SHIP_COMMIT_MESSAGE='fix: improve online menu Open Graph share cards' node ~/.cursor/ship/ship-and-report.mjs
```

If `SHIP_COMMIT_MESSAGE` is omitted, the ship script must still infer a specific subject from changed paths — never the old generic auto-release line.

## Examples

Good:
- `fix: stop menu OG share cards from returning 500 on Arabic text`
- `feat: show menu open counts by QR/WhatsApp source in branch settings`
- `docs: note menu open analytics on the system map`

Bad:
- `ship: auto release after agent work`
- `update stuff`
- `misc fixes`
